  "worked_solution": "To find the rate, we substitute $T=60$ into our equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}{|}_{T=60} & =-0.03(T-25){|}_{T=60} \\\\  & =-0.03(60-25) \\\\  & =-0.03(35) \\\\  & =-1.05\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $T={60}^{\u2218}C,$ the object's temperature decreases at a rate of $1.05$ degrees per minute.",
